  "description": "? is the second studio album by American rapper XXXTentacion, released through Bad Vibes Forever, Caroline Distribution, and Capitol Music Group on March 16, 2018. His last studio album to be released in his lifetime before his death three months later, it was primarily produced by frequent collaborator John Cunningham, includes a wide range of guest appearances from PnB Rock, Travis Barker of Blink-182, Joey Badass, Matt Ox, Rio Santana, Judah, and Carlos Andrez, and succeeds the release of his debut studio album 17 (2017) and the extended play A Ghetto Christmas Carol (2017).",
